{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991865-hearth-wisdom-useless","id":991865,"title":"hearth wisdom useless?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T08:56:56-07:00","id":991865,"title":"hearth wisdom useless?","content":"obviously it has great roleplaying potential. but im talking from a practical point of view.if one already has academics,occult,medicine what is the point of taking hearth wisdom ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:18:54-07:00","id":992008,"title":"","content":"Depends a bit on which version, but like most secondary/supplemental Abilities they're all &quot;useless.&quot; The point of them in general is to have a highly specialized Ability that lets you do X without having to have high levels of A, B, and C. Some of them provide some unique options (some versions of Hearth Wisdom have bonuses for noticing supernaturals over Occult, or allow brewing potions/etc. that actually work as extremely minor magical items).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:35:40-07:00","id":992457,"title":"","content":"We've used it in Dark Ages games to find/create weird herbal concoctions with minor mechanical effects (similar to the various drug effects in the modern game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:25:35-07:00","id":992502,"title":"","content":"Plus some of us scrub steps. That's all. /Dark Ages malk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T11:05:06-07:00","id":994112,"title":"","content":"Hearth Wisdom is knowing to plant mint in your garden to keep away invasive bugs, and specifically keep peppermint around your house to drive off rodents.<br /> Hearth Wisdom is knowing to put out grape jelly to capture a skunk, because other animals won't eat it.<br /> Hearth Wisdom is knowing to cover all the mirrors in a house when someone dies, so their soul isn't captured.<br /> Hearth Wisdom is knowing that a bowl of <i>menudo</i> will sober you up fast, or cure your cold, and that <i>abuela</i> rubbing too much Vicks on your chest cures you faster.<br /> For middle-class Americans, Hearth Wisdom is knowing that flat 7-Up and Saltines will cure an upset stomach and make you feel better.<br /> <br /> Like everything else, it's only as practical or as useless as one makes it. Hearth Wisdom captures all the things that fall through the cracks, and, honestly, <u><i>everything</i></u> was once Hearth Wisdom before it was rigorously studied and codified. Hearth Wisdom was people knowing to eat the bark of a certain tree to lessen pain, and now we have aspirin. Hearth Wisdom was people knowing to wash their clothes down river from where they burned animal sacrifices because the run-off made the clothes cleaner (a form of early lye), and now we have laundry detergent and soap.<br /> <br /> Everything starts as Hearth Wisdom and then becomes Occult, or Medicine, or Academics or whatever. It's possessing traditional or cultural knowledge or remedies that aren't covered by the above. That's <i>specifically</i> what it's for. Hearth Wisdom is knowing that, while it <i>might not</i> drive off vampires, hanging a few cloves of garlic <i>does</i> keep away mosquitoes and ticks, so fuck it - hang them anyway; it doesn't hurt (and you'll at least keep away that one vampire that has the garlic Flaw. Also, strangely enough, garlic <i>attracts</i> leeches, so it's only blood-sucking <i>bugs</i> it affects).<br /> <br /> So no, Hearth Wisdom isn't &quot;useless.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:53:31-07:00","id":996182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991865-hearth-wisdom-useless?p=994112#post994112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hearth Wisdom is knowing to plant mint in your garden to keep away invasive bugs, and specifically keep peppermint around your house to drive off rodents.<br /> Hearth Wisdom is knowing to put out grape jelly to capture a skunk, because other animals won't eat it.<br /> Hearth Wisdom is knowing to cover all the mirrors in a house when someone dies, so their soul isn't captured.<br /> Hearth Wisdom is knowing that a bowl of <i>menudo</i> will sober you up fast, or cure your cold, and that <i>abuela</i> rubbing too much Vicks on your chest cures you faster.<br /> For middle-class Americans, Hearth Wisdom is knowing that flat 7-Up and Saltines will cure an upset stomach and make you feel better.<br /> <br /> Like everything else, it's only as practical or as useless as one makes it. Hearth Wisdom captures all the things that fall through the cracks, and, honestly, <u><i>everything</i></u> was once Hearth Wisdom before it was rigorously studied and codified. Hearth Wisdom was people knowing to eat the bark of a certain tree to lessen pain, and now we have aspirin. Hearth Wisdom was people knowing to wash their clothes down river from where they burned animal sacrifices because the run-off made the clothes cleaner (a form of early lye), and now we have laundry detergent and soap.<br /> <br /> Everything starts as Hearth Wisdom and then becomes Occult, or Medicine, or Academics or whatever. It's possessing traditional or cultural knowledge or remedies that aren't covered by the above. That's <i>specifically</i> what it's for. Hearth Wisdom is knowing that, while it <i>might not</i> drive off vampires, hanging a few cloves of garlic <i>does</i> keep away mosquitoes and ticks, so fuck it - hang them anyway; it doesn't hurt (and you'll at least keep away that one vampire that has the garlic Flaw. Also, strangely enough, garlic <i>attracts</i> leeches, so it's only blood-sucking <i>bugs</i> it affects).<br /> <br /> So no, Hearth Wisdom isn't &quot;useless.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> in other hearth wisdom is like the &quot;mother&quot; of protosciences?(so to speak)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T12:11:50-08:00","id":1548373,"title":"","content":"For those who don't live that kind of life, we can't relate and so Hearth Wisdom is... hard to fathom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}